## v1.1.1
 - Suppress the GCC `stringop-overflow` false positive (`-Wno-stringop-overflow`): GCC 13/14 on aarch64 at -O3 misreports the fixed buffer in `date::detail::read`, and the release `-Werror` failed the build

## v1.1.0
 - Add the build acceleration utilities: `opendaq_target_pch`, `opendaq_target_pch_reuse`, `opendaq_target_pch_group`, `opendaq_directory_pch`, `opendaq_target_unity_tests`, `opendaq_target_unity_bindings`, `opendaq_target_unity_libs`
 - Add `OPENDAQ_ENABLE_BUILD_ACCELERATION` (ON) gating `OPENDAQ_ENABLE_PCH`, `OPENDAQ_ENABLE_UNITY_TESTS`, `OPENDAQ_ENABLE_UNITY_BINDINGS` (ON) and `OPENDAQ_ENABLE_UNITY_LIBS` (OFF), plus `OPENDAQ_UNITY_BATCH_SIZE`, to `opendaq_setup_common_build_options`
 - Make ccache work with GCC precompiled headers (`-fpch-preprocess`, sloppiness)

## v1.0.3
 - Replace the packaging utilities with staging metadata generation: the metadata is detected into `CPACK_OPENDAQ_META_*` variables, and the package name and triplet are composed from it -- `opendaq_detect_settings`, `opendaq_detect_package`, `opendaq_compose_package_triplet`, `opendaq_compose_package_file_name`, `opendaq_write_metadata`
 - Compose the package name per cpack run, through the `CPACK_OPENDAQ_PROJECT_CONFIG` project config file, so one build can yield several named packages
 - Remove `opendaq_setup_packaging`, `opendaq_generate_package_name`, `opendaq_write_staging_meta` and the post-build metadata copy

## v1.0.2
 - Add the packaging utilities: triplet detection, package naming and the staging metadata (`opendaq_detect_triplet`, `opendaq_generate_package_name`, `opendaq_detect_settings`, `opendaq_write_staging_meta`, `opendaq_setup_packaging`)
 - Include them from the project, so a consumer gets them with the rest of the utils
 - Fix the Boost alias shim when `Boost::headers` is itself an alias

## v1.0.1
 - Add target-based CMake enforcement by overriding directory-scoped commands (include_directories, add_definitions, link_directories)

## v1.0.0
 - Initial tag
